Request/cancel functions, extracted verbatim and run in node with a stub QML scope; the done-file commands they build run under bash. The sequence is summon, summon again, Escape. At the evaluated commit Menu.qml issues one done-file write, caller B exits, and caller A's done file is never created, so A keeps polling. No timing is asserted: once the menu closes nothing else can answer A. SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5 says 'cancellation reaches the caller as no-selection'. A superseded prompt is dismissed without an answer, which violates it. SW-REQ-260922-50RE (open dispatch) does not say what happens to an in-flight request, so supersession is a spec gap below X6Z5. Base choice: fork quattro head 020a8c0e, which contains the upstream product head b18ab495 plus the spec corpus. The defect is present there and at b18ab495 (comparative run). Fix: upstream PR omacom/omarchy#9056 (open() answers the in-flight request via finishRequest(null)); the reproducer passes on its fork mirror pr/9056 and on fork branch fix/issue-9057-menu-select-poll, which also bounds the poll. KI-MENU-SELECT-POLL-DEADLOCK (same unbounded poll, but triggered by the menu process dying) is related: same entry point and same observable, different trigger and requirement (SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS).","validationDigest":"sha256:0ac134f99a084876cd7bda8303e3f4457dd5635317a7c16dbab78592ca321310","validationId":"rval-ece2f65569e060bd869ef72f636194d8","verdict":"confirmed"}
